            <ArticleTitle>Once a post-dural puncture headache patient always post-dural puncture headache patient?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>167-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>It is well known that symptoms of post-dural puncture headache (PDPH) are more likely if there has been a preceding PDPH. We herein present a patient who developed a PDPH following each of two dural punctures separated by 9 years.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
